  [1mTesting.[0m The core is environment-agnostic and takes an injected sink and clock, so all of it tests with an array-push
  sink and a fixed timestamp — no DOM, no subprocess, no fixtures. Worth covering: level threshold filtering, allowlist
  drops and the [38;5;153m_dropped[39m list, primitive coercion, truncation, [38;5;153mresolveLevel[39m ordering and fallback, the [38;5;153mlogger.bad_level[39m
  warning, and sink-throw containment. That last one matters most: it's the test that proves a broken transport can't
  take down the login form.

